Package: darpan
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Darpan maintainers <maintainers@darpan.invalid>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly, libx11-6, libxext6, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxtst6, xclip, x11-xserver-utils, systemd
Recommends: gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1
Conflicts: porthole
Replaces: porthole
Description: fast, private remote desktop host
 Darpan lets you use this computer from your other devices, in a browser
 or a native app. The screen is captured only when it changes and encoded on
 the NVIDIA GPU (NVENC), so it costs next to nothing while the machine trains
 models. Connections travel end-to-end encrypted over a bundled, unprivileged
 Tailscale; nothing is exposed to the internet and no root daemon is added.
